<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL RAISES GASOLINE PRICES ON WEDNESDAY.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL RAISES GASOLINE PRICES ON WEDNESDAY.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland BV said on Monday it would raise its retail prices for gasoline in the Netherlands by one cent per litre with effect from Wednesday, July 23.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, the company said. It added that diesel prices would remain unchanged.</p>
<p>From Wednesday the price of premium unleaded gasoline at Shell's self-service stations will rise to 2.24 guilders per litre. The price of premium with lead substitute goes up to 2.31 guilders and that of Euro regular unleaded to 2.19 guilders.</p>
<p>The recommended price for diesel remains at 1.516 guilders per litre, Shell said.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
